2	//! they are the `userPrompt` of a randomly-named, exported Piton anchor whose
3	//! imports `piton lsp` adds automatically (see [`crate::piton_lsp`]), so they
4	//! are never written or seen. Each sent prompt is saved as a `.pi` file in the
5	//! project's prompt history and compiled; the harness receives the prompt with
6	//! each reference in it resolved.
