8	//! A prompt may hold anything, pasted text included, so it isn't written as
9	//! Piton prose, where braces, colons, leading dashes, comments, and
10	//! backslashes all mean something. It is written in a multi-line escape block
11	//! instead, which Piton keeps exactly as it is. Each `@{Name}` or
12	//! `${Name.path}` in it whose name is imported is also listed, once, in the
13	//! anchor's `references`, which is what `piton compile` resolves; the prompt's
14	//! text around them is taken from the saved source. A reference to a name
